{"type":"message","id":"a3d8b942","parentId":"1a2fe68a","timestamp":"2026-05-16T00:04:23.260Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So `origin/master` is at `7a2a46a1 auto backup 2026-05-15`, which is the previous backup. Our current commit `27837268 auto backup 2026-05-16` is NOT on the remote yet. The push did NOT succeed.\n\nThe problem seems to be that `git push` gets killed by SIGTERM before completing. This is very strange. Let me think about what could cause this.\n\nWait - could this be an issue with the SSH agent or git credential helper? When `git push` hangs, it might be waiting for user input (like a password or confirmation), but since it's non-interactive, it just hangs until killed.\n\nLet me try using `GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0` and ensure SSH is set up properly:\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\nRemote is still on `2026-05-15` - push didn't go through. The `git push` is hanging. Let me diagnose the SSH issue:\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-f6152832-2455-4e4b-8cce-3dc37c2bb7d0","name":"exec","arguments":{"timeout":10,"command":"cd ~/.openclaw && GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0 SSH_AUTH_SOCK=/tmp/ssh-auth.sock ssh -o ConnectTimeout=5 -T git@github.com 2>&1 | head -5"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":1501,"output":279,"cacheRead":27248,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":29028,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1778889857585,"responseId":"chatcmpl-368437f8-e5cb-4b2c-b85e-89439c496eab"}}
