{"type":"message","id":"018e6675","parentId":"818b7050","timestamp":"2026-05-16T00:04:53.502Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me poll to see what's happening.\n\nActually wait - I should think about this differently. The `exec` tool seems to have some process management that kills processes after a certain time or under certain conditions. Each time I run `git push` it gets killed with SIGTERM.\n\nLet me try a completely different approach - use the `background=true` parameter to run it in background, and then check the result later.\n\nActually, thinking about it more - maybe the issue is that git push is trying to pack a large number of objects and it's the packing that's slow. Or maybe there's a git config issue.\n\nLet me try a background push:\n\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-a0c0776c-8743-4656-a844-f331c998067e","name":"process","arguments":{"timeout":18000,"action":"poll","sessionId":"gentle-kelp"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":125,"output":179,"cacheRead":29136,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":29440,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1778889882849,"responseId":"chatcmpl-333815e8-a2e7-4707-8363-393a41f194d5"}}
