{"type":"message","id":"b6e83b3f","parentId":"2cd25c2f","timestamp":"2026-05-16T00:05:22.107Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"OK, so now I have a timeout of 120 seconds. Let me poll and see if it completes. This should be enough time for the push to complete.\n\nBut wait - I should note that the exec tool has a maximum timeout limit. Let me see if 120 seconds works or if it still gets killed.\n\nActually, the `timeout` command itself will kill the process after 120 seconds. The `exec` tool has a `timeout` parameter of 125 seconds. These should align.\n\nLet me poll after a good amount of time.\n\nActually, I should think about what files are being pushed. The commit was `27837268 auto backup 2026-05-16`. What files did it include? Let me check which files are in that commit:\n\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-ad539611-3026-4e80-afbc-156311d20dd7","name":"process","arguments":{"action":"poll","sessionId":"ember-prairie","timeout":120000}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":1632,"output":206,"cacheRead":28368,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":30206,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1778889910506,"responseId":"chatcmpl-e98fd979-db91-4beb-b00b-a6419ab7f9c6"}}
